Package: glmmplanr
Title: Two-Dimensional Sample Size Planning for Crossed Binary GLMMs
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Ryuya", "Komuro", , "ryuya.komuro.c4@tohoku.ac.jp", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An end-to-end sample size and precision optimization pipeline for
    crossed binary Generalized Linear Mixed Models (GLMMs) and Explanatory Item
    Response Models in behavioral science, psycholinguistics, and language
    assessment. Generates balanced Latin-square, between-within, incomplete-block,
    and testlet-nested designs with configurable factor contrasts; numerically
    inverts marginal cell probabilities and m-AFC guessing asymptotes into
    conditional GLMM parameters via two-dimensional Gauss-Hermite quadrature;
    evaluates statistical power, confidence/credible interval width (AIPE),
    ROPE exclusion, singularity/convergence rates, coverage, and Type M/S
    errors; and identifies non-dominated Pareto-optimal (N_subj x N_item)
    designs using Universal Kriging monotone Gaussian process surrogates and
    multi-stage parallel C++ estimation. Supports both random-item and fixed-bank
    Rasch parameter recovery planning.
